From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: size the CWB list by the CWB blocks an encoder
 can hold

dpu_encoder_virt_atomic_mode_set() collects the assigned CWB blocks in a
local array of MAX_CHANNELS_PER_ENC entries and copies them into
dpu_enc->hw_cwb[], which has MAX_CWB_PER_ENC (2). With
MAX_CHANNELS_PER_ENC raised to 4 for quad-pipe topologies, four CWB
blocks could be returned and written past the end of hw_cwb[].

Size the local array by MAX_CWB_PER_ENC, so the resource manager
returns at most as many blocks as the encoder can hold, as before.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index 3b50cbb6e92..0f3e4e64791 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -1181,7 +1181,7 @@ static void dpu_encoder_virt_atomic_mode_set(struct drm_encoder *drm_enc,
 	struct dpu_hw_blk *hw_pp[MAX_CHANNELS_PER_ENC];
 	struct dpu_hw_blk *hw_ctl[MAX_CHANNELS_PER_ENC];
 	struct dpu_hw_blk *hw_dsc[MAX_CHANNELS_PER_ENC];
-	struct dpu_hw_blk *hw_cwb[MAX_CHANNELS_PER_ENC];
+	struct dpu_hw_blk *hw_cwb[MAX_CWB_PER_ENC];
 	int num_ctl, num_pp, num_dsc, num_pp_per_intf;
 	int num_cwb = 0;
 	bool is_cwb_encoder;
-- 
